IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `sgia-interpretation-time`
IMPORT `sgia-p4-powers`

-- Tests for sgia-p4-powers.l4 (ss 27 to 37). Expected values are written from the text of each section.

§ `s 27`

#ASSERT `the power may be exercised and the duty must be performed from time to time as occasion requires` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `the power may be exercised and the duty must be performed from time to time as occasion requires` TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `the power may be exercised and the duty must be performed from time to time as occasion requires` FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `the person may exercise the power or must perform the duty` TRUE `the holder of the office for the time being` FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `the person may exercise the power or must perform the duty` TRUE `a person duly appointed to act for the holder` FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `the person may exercise the power or must perform the duty` TRUE `someone else` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `the person may exercise the power or must perform the duty` FALSE `the holder of the office for the time being` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `the person may exercise the power or must perform the duty` TRUE `the holder of the office for the time being` TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `the power includes this, exercisable in like manner and subject to the like consent and conditions` TRUE `the power to amend` FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `the power includes this, exercisable in like manner and subject to the like consent and conditions` TRUE `the power to vary` FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `the power includes this, exercisable in like manner and subject to the like consent and conditions` TRUE `the power to rescind` FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `the power includes this, exercisable in like manner and subject to the like consent and conditions` TRUE `the power to revoke` FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `the power includes this, exercisable in like manner and subject to the like consent and conditions` TRUE `the power to suspend` FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `the power includes this, exercisable in like manner and subject to the like consent and conditions` TRUE `the power to abstain from doing the act` FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `the power includes this, exercisable in like manner and subject to the like consent and conditions` TRUE `something else` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `the power includes this, exercisable in like manner and subject to the like consent and conditions` TRUE `the power to amend` TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `the power includes this, exercisable in like manner and subject to the like consent and conditions` FALSE `the power to amend` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

§ `s 28`

#ASSERT `the power to appoint includes this` TRUE `the power to dismiss a person appointed` FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `the power to appoint includes this` TRUE `the power to suspend a person appointed` FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `the power to appoint includes this` TRUE `the power to appoint another person temporarily in place of a person suspended` FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `the power to appoint includes this` TRUE `the power to appoint another person temporarily in place of a sick or absent holder` FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `the power to appoint includes this` TRUE `something else` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `the power to appoint includes this` TRUE `the power to dismiss a person appointed` TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `the power to appoint includes this` FALSE `the power to dismiss a person appointed` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `the power of dismissal is exercisable` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `the power of dismissal is exercisable` TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `the power of dismissal is exercisable` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `the power of dismissal is exercisable` FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

§ `s 29`

#ASSERT `the power is understood to be also conferred` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `the power is understood to be also conferred` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `the power is understood to be also conferred` FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `the power includes this, without limiting section 29(1)` `a power to prohibit, control or regulate a matter` `power to provide for the matter by licensing it` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `the power includes this, without limiting section 29(1)` `a power to prohibit, control or regulate a matter` `power to prohibit acts whereby the prohibitions, control or regulations might be evaded` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `the power includes this, without limiting section 29(1)` `a power to prohibit, control or regulate a matter` `power to impose reasonable conditions subject to which the licence, permit, authority, approval or exemption may be granted` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `the power includes this, without limiting section 29(1)` `a power to grant a licence, permit, authority, approval or exemption` `power to impose reasonable conditions subject to which the licence, permit, authority, approval or exemption may be granted` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `the power includes this, without limiting section 29(1)` `a power to grant a licence, permit, authority, approval or exemption` `power to provide for the matter by licensing it` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `the power includes this, without limiting section 29(1)` `some other power` `something else` EQUALS NOTHING

§ `ss 30, 31, 32`

#ASSERT `the appointment is made in a way section 30 allows` TRUE `by naming a person` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `the appointment is made in a way section 30 allows` TRUE `by directing the person for the time being holding a designated office` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `the appointment is made in a way section 30 allows` TRUE `some other way` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `the appointment is made in a way section 30 allows` FALSE `by naming a person` EQUALS NOTHING
-- s 30(3): not earlier than the commencement of the Act
#ASSERT `the appointment may be made with retrospective effect to that date` (Date 1 1 2020) (Date 1 1 2020)
#ASSERT NOT (`the appointment may be made with retrospective effect to that date` (Date 31 12 2019) (Date 1 1 2020))
#ASSERT `the appointment may be made with retrospective effect to that date` (Date 2 1 2020) (Date 1 1 2020)
#ASSERT `the public officer referred to includes this officer` TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`the public officer referred to includes this officer` TRUE FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT (`the public officer referred to includes this officer` FALSE TRUE)
#ASSERT `the day from which the appointment may be declared to have effect` (Date 1 1 2020) (Date 1 1 2020) EQUALS JUST (Date 1 1 2020)
#ASSERT `the day from which the appointment may be declared to have effect` (Date 31 12 2019) (Date 1 1 2020) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `the day from which the appointment may be declared to have effect` (Date 1 6 2020) (Date 1 1 2020) EQUALS JUST (Date 1 6 2020)

§ `s 32A: majority, quorum, casting vote`

#ASSERT `is a statutory body for section 32A` TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`is a statutory body for section 32A` TRUE FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT (`is a statutory body for section 32A` FALSE TRUE)
-- majority of 3 or more: more than half of all the persons
#ASSERT `the power may be exercised or the function or duty performed by a majority of those persons` 3 2 FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `the power may be exercised or the function or duty performed by a majority of those persons` 3 1 FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `the power may be exercised or the function or duty performed by a majority of those persons` 4 2 FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `the power may be exercised or the function or duty performed by a majority of those persons` 4 3 FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `the power may be exercised or the function or duty performed by a majority of those persons` 2 2 FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `the power may be exercised or the function or duty performed by a majority of those persons` 3 3 TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
-- quorum: fixed number 9 -> at least half of that number (4.5): 5 present, not 4
#ASSERT `a quorum is constituted at the meeting` 9 (JUST 9) 9 5 FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `a quorum is constituted at the meeting` 9 (JUST 9) 9 4 FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `a quorum is constituted at the meeting` 8 (JUST 8) 8 4 FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `a quorum is constituted at the meeting` 8 (JUST 8) 8 3 FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- number not fixed (a range): at least half of the members in office (7 in office: 4, not 3)
#ASSERT `a quorum is constituted at the meeting` 7 NOTHING 7 4 FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `a quorum is constituted at the meeting` 7 NOTHING 7 3 FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `a quorum is constituted at the meeting` 7 NOTHING 6 3 FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `a quorum is constituted at the meeting` 2 (JUST 2) 2 1 FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `a quorum is constituted at the meeting` 7 NOTHING 7 4 TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
-- act of the majority of those present, if they are a quorum
#ASSERT `the act or thing is regarded as done by the body` 5 TRUE 5 3 FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `the act or thing is regarded as done by the body` 5 TRUE 5 2 FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `the act or thing is regarded as done by the body` 5 FALSE 5 5 FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `the act or thing is regarded as done by the body` 2 TRUE 2 2 FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `the act or thing is regarded as done by the body` 5 TRUE 5 3 TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
-- fork F23: on the same facts (a body of 5, three present who are a quorum, two of the three agree) (2)(b) says yes and (1) says no; no rule combines them
#ASSERT `the act or thing is regarded as done by the body` 5 TRUE 3 2 FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `the power may be exercised or the function or duty performed by a majority of those persons` 5 2 FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- (3) casting vote
#ASSERT `the chairperson or other member presiding has a casting as well as a deliberative vote` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `the chairperson or other member presiding has a casting as well as a deliberative vote` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `the chairperson or other member presiding has a casting as well as a deliberative vote` TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `the chairperson or other member presiding has a casting as well as a deliberative vote` FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

§ `ss 33, 33A`

#ASSERT `the powers of the body are affected` TRUE `a vacancy in the membership` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `the powers of the body are affected` TRUE `a defect later discovered in the appointment or qualification of a person purporting to be a member` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `the powers of the body are affected` TRUE `a minor irregularity in convening a meeting` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `the powers of the body are affected` TRUE `something else` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `the powers of the body are affected` TRUE `a vacancy in the membership` TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `the powers of the body are affected` FALSE `a vacancy in the membership` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `the body may invest the moneys in the manner it thinks fit, and engage in financial activity or arrangements to manage or hedge risk from the investment` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `the body may invest the moneys in the manner it thinks fit, and engage in financial activity or arrangements to manage or hedge risk from the investment` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `the body may invest the moneys in the manner it thinks fit, and engage in financial activity or arrangements to manage or hedge risk from the investment` FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

§ `ss 34, 35, 35A, 37: signified, signed`

#ASSERT `the exercise of the President's power is sufficiently signified` `any Minister` FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `the exercise of the President's power is sufficiently signified` `the Secretary to the Cabinet` FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `the exercise of the President's power is sufficiently signified` `someone else` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `the exercise of the President's power is sufficiently signified` `any Minister` TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `the exercise of the President's power is sufficiently signified` `the President himself or herself` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `the exercise of the Minister's power is sufficiently signified` `the Permanent Secretary to the Ministry for which the Minister is responsible` FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `the exercise of the Minister's power is sufficiently signified` `a public officer duly authorised in writing by the Minister` FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `the exercise of the Minister's power is sufficiently signified` `someone else` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `the exercise of the Minister's power is sufficiently signified` `the Permanent Secretary to the Ministry for which the Minister is responsible` TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `the power to delegate extends to making subsidiary legislation` TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `the power to delegate extends to making subsidiary legislation` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `the exercise of the statutory body's power to make subsidiary legislation is sufficiently signified` `the chairperson of the statutory body` FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `the exercise of the statutory body's power to make subsidiary legislation is sufficiently signified` `a member of the statutory body duly authorised by it to do so in place of the chairperson` FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `the exercise of the statutory body's power to make subsidiary legislation is sufficiently signified` `someone else` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `the exercise of the statutory body's power to make subsidiary legislation is sufficiently signified` `the chairperson of the statutory body` TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `the requirement that a document be under the hand of or countersigned by a Minister is met` `the Permanent Secretary to the Ministry for which the Minister is responsible` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `the requirement that a document be under the hand of or countersigned by a Minister is met` `a public officer duly authorised in writing by the Minister` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `the requirement that a document be under the hand of or countersigned by a Minister is met` `any Minister` EQUALS NOTHING

§ `s 36: delegation of functions of Minister`

-- (2): to a Minister, Minister of State or Parliamentary Secretary assigned by the Prime Minister: with the Prime Minister's approval
#ASSERT `the delegation is permitted by section 36` TRUE `a function` `a Minister, Minister of State or Parliamentary Secretary assigned by the Prime Minister to assist the responsible Minister` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `the delegation is permitted by section 36` TRUE `a function` `a Minister, Minister of State or Parliamentary Secretary assigned by the Prime Minister to assist the responsible Minister` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `the delegation is permitted by section 36` TRUE `a function` `a Minister, Minister of State or Parliamentary Secretary assigned by the Prime Minister to assist the responsible Minister` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- (3): to a public body or public officer, unless the contrary intention appears in an Act
#ASSERT `the delegation is permitted by section 36` TRUE `a function` `a public body or a public officer` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `the delegation is permitted by section 36` TRUE `a function` `a public body or a public officer` FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `the delegation is permitted by section 36` TRUE `a function` `someone else` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- (6): not a power to make subsidiary legislation, nor the power of delegation; (7): no further delegation
#ASSERT `the delegation is permitted by section 36` TRUE `a power to make subsidiary legislation` `a public body or a public officer` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `the delegation is permitted by section 36` TRUE `the power of delegation in section 36` `a public body or a public officer` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `the delegation is permitted by section 36` TRUE `a function` `a public body or a public officer` TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- (1): only where an Act confers or imposes the function on a Minister
#ASSERT `the delegation is permitted by section 36` FALSE `a function` `a public body or a public officer` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `the delegate may exercise the function based on the delegate's own opinion, belief or state of mind` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `the delegate may exercise the function based on the delegate's own opinion, belief or state of mind` TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `the delegate may exercise the function based on the delegate's own opinion, belief or state of mind` FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `section 36(5) says a delegation` `made by order in the Gazette` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `section 36(5) says a delegation` `general or limited` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `section 36(5) says a delegation` `subject to conditions consistent with the nature of the delegated function` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `section 36(5) says a delegation` `to a named person or to the holder of an office` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `section 36(5) says a delegation` `to 2 or more persons at the same time` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `section 36(5) says a delegation` `preventing the responsible Minister from personally exercising the delegated function` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `section 36(5) says a delegation` `something else` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `the delegation meets the requirement of form in section 36(5)(a)` TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`the delegation meets the requirement of form in section 36(5)(a)` FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT (`section 36 affects the operation of that rule of law` TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT (`in section 36 a reference to an Act includes subsidiary legislation made under the Act` TRUE)
